course: dictionary
lesson: 16164
title: One word, two meanings: worshipped
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Worshipped is the past of worship. Its first meaning is to show love, praise and honour to God or a god, by praying, singing and going to services. «The villagers worshipped in the old stone church every Sunday.»
explain: Worshipped can also mean loved and admired very much. Nobody is praying here. «The whole town worshipped the local footballer.» It means the town thought he was wonderful. «She worshipped the ground her grandad walked on.» This shows she loved him very much.
explain: To know which meaning is right, read the words around it. If the sentence is about church, prayer or God, it means honour to God. If it is about a fan or a hero, it means loved and admired. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Worship means showing love, praise and honour to God or a god.
fact: «Worshipped» is the past of worship, so it tells you what happened before now.
fact: «Worshipped» can mean loved and admired very much, as in «a worshipped footballer».
fact: An idol is a statue or object that people treat as a false god.
fact: Christians worship in churches, Jews in synagogues, Muslims in mosques and Hindus in temples.
fact: Ancient Egyptians worshipped many gods, such as Ra, the Sun god.
exercise: «The villagers worshipped in the old stone church every Sunday.» What does worshipped mean here? | Shouted loudly at the church door | *Showed love and praise to God by praying and singing | Cleaned all the church windows | Built a new bell tower
exercise: «The whole town worshipped the local footballer.» What does worshipped mean? | *Loved and admired very much | Waited for him to sign a contract | Hated and ignored | Watched him sleep
exercise: Which word is the past of worship? | worship | worships | worshipping | *worshipped
test: What kind of gods were worshipped in ancient Egypt? | Football players and singers | *Many gods, such as Ra the Sun god | Gods who lived only in the sea | Only one god, who had a beard
test: «The people worshipped idols, so they were told to turn back to God.» What is an idol? | *A statue of a false god | A loud singer | A type of bird | A kind of church bell
exam: «Her little brother worshipped the ground she walked on.» What does this mean? | He had never met her | He wanted to dig up the garden | *He loved and admired her very much | He was afraid of her
